§§ `A single resident employee, income year 2025 (YA 2026)`

-- A1: $5,000 a month, born 1995 (aged 30). CPF 20% of 5,000 = 1,000 a month, 12,000. Reliefs: earned income $1,000 (s 39(1)(a)); CPF 12,000
-- (s 39(2)(ga)(ii), (10A)(b): over $5,000 so exactly the CPF). Chargeable 60,000 - 13,000 = 47,000. Tax by Table 3: 0 on 20,000, 2% of 10,000 = 200,
-- 3.5% of 10,000 = 350, 7% of 7,000 = 490: 1,040. Net 60,000 - 1,040 - 12,000 = 46,960.
#ASSERT `the income tax of` `A1` EQUALS 1040

#ASSERT `the employee CPF of` `A1` EQUALS 12000

#ASSERT `the net income of` `A1` EQUALS 46960
-- A2: 100,000 a year, paid evenly: $8,333.33 a month, above the 2025 Ordinary Wage Ceiling of $7,400: CPF 20% of 7,400 = 1,480 a month = 17,760.
-- Reliefs 1,000 + 17,760 = 18,760; chargeable 81,240. Tax: 3,350 on the first 80,000 (200 + 350 + 7% of 40,000) + 11.5% of 1,240 = 142.60: 3,492.60.
-- Net 100,000 - 3,492.60 - 17,760 = 78,747.40.
#ASSERT `the income tax of` `A2` EQUALS (3492 + 0.6)

#ASSERT `the employee CPF of` `A2` EQUALS 17760

#ASSERT `the net income of` `A2` EQUALS (78747 + 0.4)
-- A3: $1,500 a month. CPF 300 a month, 3,600. Chargeable 18,000 - 1,000 - 3,600 = 13,400: under the 20,000 nil band.
#ASSERT `the income tax of` `A3` EQUALS 0

#ASSERT `the employee CPF of` `A3` EQUALS 3600

#ASSERT `the net income of` `A3` EQUALS 14400
-- A4: $2,500 a month. CPF 500 a month, 6,000. Reliefs 1,000 + 6,000; chargeable 30,000 - 7,000 = 23,000: 2% of 3,000 = 60. Net 30,000 - 60 - 6,000.
#ASSERT `the income tax of` `A4` EQUALS 60

#ASSERT `the net income of` `A4` EQUALS 23940
-- A5: born 1969 (aged 56 at 31 December 2025; 55th birthday in 2024, in the above-55 CPF band all of 2025): CPF 17% of 5,000 = 850 a month = 10,200.
-- Earned income relief $6,000 (s 39(1)(c)). Reliefs 16,200; chargeable 43,800: 550 on the first 40,000 + 7% of 3,800 = 266: 816. Net 60,000 - 816 - 10,200.
#ASSERT `the income tax of` `A5` EQUALS 816

#ASSERT `the employee CPF of` `A5` EQUALS 10200

#ASSERT `the net income of` `A5` EQUALS 48984
-- A6: born December 1970: 55 on 31 December 2025, so the CPF band for 2025 is still 55-and-below (the older band starts the month after the birthday
-- month, January 2026): CPF 12,000. Earned income relief $6,000 (fork I3: aged at least 55 at 31 December). Reliefs 18,000; chargeable 42,000:
-- 550 + 7% of 2,000 = 140: 690. Net 60,000 - 690 - 12,000 = 47,310.
#ASSERT `the income tax of` `A6` EQUALS 690

#ASSERT `the employee CPF of` `A6` EQUALS 12000

#ASSERT `the net income of` `A6` EQUALS 47310
-- A7: born December 1964 (61 at 31 December 2025; 60 in December 2024): CPF band above 60 to 65, 11.5% of 5,000 = 575 a month = 6,900.
-- Earned income relief $8,000 (s 39(1)(d)). Reliefs 14,900; chargeable 45,100: 550 + 7% of 5,100 = 357: 907. Net 60,000 - 907 - 6,900 = 52,193.
#ASSERT `the income tax of` `A7` EQUALS 907

#ASSERT `the employee CPF of` `A7` EQUALS 6900

#ASSERT `the net income of` `A7` EQUALS 52193
-- A8: $5,000 a month and a $10,000 bonus in December (wages 70,000). The room under 102,000 after 60,000 of ordinary wages is 42,000, so the whole bonus
-- counts: CPF 12,000 + 20% of 10,000 = 14,000. Reliefs 1,000 + 14,000; chargeable 55,000: 550 + 7% of 15,000 = 1,050: 1,600. Net 70,000 - 1,600 - 14,000.
#ASSERT `the income tax of` `A8` EQUALS 1600

#ASSERT `the employee CPF of` `A8` EQUALS 14000

#ASSERT `the net income of` `A8` EQUALS 54400

§§ `A married couple: the spouse relief and its $8,000 limit`

-- B1: the earner of A2 and a spouse whose income is exactly $8,000 (s 39(2)(a): "not more than $8,000", YA 2025 or later). The earner's chargeable income is
-- 81,240 - 2,000 = 79,240: 3,350 - 7% of 760 (53.20) = 3,296.80. The spouse: wages 8,000, CPF 0.6 x (666.67 - 500) = 100 a month, 1,200; reliefs 1,000 + 1,200;
-- chargeable 5,800: no tax. Household 3,296.80.
#ASSERT `the income tax of` `B1` EQUALS (3296 + 0.8)
-- B2: the spouse's income is $8,001: the relief is lost. The earner pays 3,492.60 (A2); the spouse still nothing. The cliff is 3,492.60 - 3,296.80 = 195.80.
#ASSERT `the income tax of` `B2` EQUALS (3492 + 0.6)
-- B3 (fork H1): a spouse with no work whose bank interest and dividends total $9,000. The Act does not define "income" in s 39(2)(a); IRAS counts tax-exempt
-- income, and so does this encoding: no spouse relief, so the earner pays 3,492.60. Under the other reading ("income" is assessable income only) the earner
-- would pay 3,296.80, as in B4.
#ASSERT `the income tax of` `B3` EQUALS (3492 + 0.6)
-- B4: a spouse with no income at all: spouse relief $2,000, earner 3,296.80.
#ASSERT `the income tax of` `B4` EQUALS (3296 + 0.8)
-- B1 again, its employee CPF: the earner 17,760 and the spouse 1,200 (OW 666.67: 0.6 x 166.67 = 100.00 a month, the fraction ignored).
#ASSERT `the employee CPF of` `B1` EQUALS 18960

§§ `Children: the qualifying child relief, the working mother's child relief, the parenthood rebate`

-- C1: the A1 earner with one child born in 2018 who is below 16, maintained, with no income. Qualifying child relief $4,000 (Fifth Schedule para 1), all hers.
-- Chargeable 60,000 - 1,000 - 12,000 - 4,000 = 43,000: 550 + 7% of 3,000 = 210: 760. Net 60,000 - 760 - 12,000 = 47,240.
#ASSERT `the income tax of` `C1` EQUALS 760

#ASSERT `the net income of` `C1` EQUALS 47240
-- C2: a child born in 2009 turns 16 during 2025, so was "below 16 years of age at any time during the year" (s 39(2)(e)(i)): relief $4,000, tax 760.
#ASSERT `the income tax of` `C2` EQUALS 760
-- C3: a child born in 2008 turned 16 in 2024, was not below 16 at any time in 2025, and is not in full-time instruction: no relief, tax 1,040.
#ASSERT `the income tax of` `C3` EQUALS 1040
-- C4: the same child in full-time instruction (s 39(2)(e)(ii)): relief $4,000, tax 760.
#ASSERT `the income tax of` `C4` EQUALS 760
-- C5: a child with income of $9,000 (more than $8,000, YA 2025 or later, Fifth Schedule para 3B): no relief: 1,040.
#ASSERT `the income tax of` `C5` EQUALS 1040
-- C6: income exactly $8,000: relief $4,000: 760.
#ASSERT `the income tax of` `C6` EQUALS 760
-- C7: income $9,000 but incapacitated: para 3B does not bar it; the relief is $7,500 (s 39(2)(e)(v)): chargeable 60,000 - 13,000 - 7,500 = 39,500: 200 + 350 + 3.5% of... computed: 20,000 nil; 10,000 at 2% = 200; 9,500 at 3.5% = 332.50: 532.50.
#ASSERT `the income tax of` `C7` EQUALS (532 + 0.5)
-- C8: two children shared equally by the parents. The first adult (5,000 a month): CPF 12,000; relief 1,000 + 12,000 + 2 x (4,000 x 1/2) = 17,000; chargeable 43,000:
-- 760. The second (3,000 a month): CPF 600 x 12 = 7,200; reliefs 1,000 + 7,200 + 4,000 = 12,200; chargeable 36,000 - 12,200 = 23,800: 2% of 3,800 = 76. Neither
-- has a woman claimant, no spouse relief (the other's income is over 8,000). Household 836.
#ASSERT `the income tax of` `C8` EQUALS 836
-- C9: a married mother (first adult, 5,000 a month) and a father (7,000 a month); one child born 2018, hers to claim wholly. The mother: CPF 12,000; working
-- mother's child relief 15% of her earned income 60,000 = 9,000 (Fifth Schedule para 5(1A)(c): the date is before 1 January 2024); qualifying child relief 4,000; earned income
-- relief 1,000; reliefs 26,000; chargeable 34,000: 10,000 at 2% = 200 and 4,000 at 3.5% = 140: 340.
-- The father: CPF 20% of 7,000 = 1,400 a month = 16,800; reliefs 1,000 + 16,800; chargeable 84,000 - 17,800 = 66,200: 550 + 7% of 26,200 = 1,834: 2,384. Household 2,724.
#ASSERT `the income tax of` `C9` EQUALS 2724

#ASSERT `the employee CPF of` `C9` EQUALS 28800

#ASSERT `the net income of` `C9` EQUALS 112476
-- C13: as C9, but the father claims all of the qualifying child relief (the first adult's share is 0). The mother still maintains the child, so she keeps the working
-- mother's child relief: 15% of 60,000 = 9,000. Mother: reliefs 1,000 + 12,000 + 9,000 = 22,000; chargeable 38,000: 200 + 8,000 x 3.5% = 280: 480. Father: reliefs 1,000 +
-- 16,800 + 4,000 = 21,800; chargeable 62,200: 550 + 22,200 x 7% = 1,554: 2,104. Household 2,584.
#ASSERT `the income tax of` `C13` EQUALS 2584
-- C10: the same, a child born in 2024: working mother's child relief $8,000 (Fifth Schedule para 5(1AB)(c): date on or after 1 January 2024). Her reliefs 1,000 + 12,000 +
-- 4,000 + 8,000 = 25,000; chargeable 35,000: 10,000 at 2% = 200 and 5,000 at 3.5% = 175: 375. Household 375 + 2,384 = 2,759. The child was born in 2024, so no
-- parenthood rebate in YA 2026 (it was for YA 2025).
#ASSERT `the income tax of` `C10` EQUALS 2759
-- C11: a father on 5,000 a month with a first child born in 2025 (a citizen): s 42A(2A) rebate $5,000 against the tax for YA 2026. His tax before the rebate: qualifying
-- child relief 4,000 gives chargeable 43,000: 760. The rebate exceeds it: tax 0, and 4,240 carried forward (s 42A(3)). Net 60,000 - 0 - 12,000.
#ASSERT `the income tax of` `C11` EQUALS 0

#ASSERT `the net income of` `C11` EQUALS 48000
-- C12: the 2025 baby is the second child: rebate $10,000 (s 42A(1)). Reliefs: 2 x 4,000; chargeable 60,000 - 13,000 - 8,000 = 39,000: 200 + 9,000 x 3.5% = 315: 515; the rebate absorbs it: 0.
#ASSERT `the income tax of` `C12` EQUALS 0

§§ `Parents, insurance, SRS and the $80,000 cap`

-- D1: a parent aged 70 living with the claimant (income 3,000) $9,000, and a parent aged 65 living apart, maintained with $2,500 (income 0) $5,500 (s 39(2)(i)(iv)).
-- Reliefs 1,000 + 12,000 + 14,500 = 27,500; chargeable 32,500: 200 + 2,500 x 3.5% = 87.50: 287.50.
#ASSERT `the income tax of` `D1` EQUALS (287 + 0.5)
-- D2: born 1959 (66): CPF 7.5% of 5,000 = 375 a month = 4,500; earned income relief 8,000; life insurance premiums 2,000. CPF 4,500 and premiums 6,500 exceed the $5,000
-- cap of s 39(10A)(b) (the contributions are not over $5,000): the relief is 5,000. Reliefs 13,000; chargeable 47,000: 1,040. Net 60,000 - 1,040 - 4,500 = 54,460.
#ASSERT `the income tax of` `D2` EQUALS 1040

#ASSERT `the net income of` `D2` EQUALS 54460
-- D3: 50,000 a month (600,000 a year), SRS $15,300, CPF top-ups 8,000 for herself and 8,000 for family, two incapacitated parents living with her (2 x 14,000), four
-- children (4 x 4,000). CPF 1,480 x 12 = 17,760. Reliefs before the cap: 1,000 + 17,760 + 15,300 + 8,000 + 8,000 + 28,000 + 16,000 = 94,060: capped at $80,000 (s 39A).
-- Chargeable 520,000. Tax: 84,150 on the first 500,000 + 23% of 20,000 = 4,600: 88,750.
#ASSERT `the income tax of` `D3` EQUALS 88750

#ASSERT `the employee CPF of` `D3` EQUALS 17760

§§ `Where the encoding does not answer, and income year 2026`

-- E1: an adult who is not resident for income tax: not covered (-1).
#ASSERT `the income tax of` `E1` EQUALS (-1)
-- E2: a permanent resident in the first two years (graduated CPF rates, paragraphs 1A to 1D): not covered.
#ASSERT `the income tax of` `E2` EQUALS (-1)
-- E3: income year 2024: not covered.
#ASSERT `the income tax of` `E3` EQUALS (-1)
-- E4: a sole adult with half of a child's relief: the other half belongs to nobody, which no division of the relief makes (fork H2): not covered.
#ASSERT `the income tax of` `E4` EQUALS (-1)
-- E5: the same for the parenthood rebate's share: not covered.
#ASSERT `the income tax of` `E5` EQUALS (-1)
-- E6: a share of more than the whole (1.5): not covered, whoever the second adult is.
#ASSERT `the income tax of` `E6` EQUALS (-1)
-- E7: a negative share: not covered.
#ASSERT `the income tax of` `E7` EQUALS (-1)
-- F1: income year 2026 (YA 2027), $5,000 a month: CPF 20% of 5,000 = 1,000 (the 2026 Ordinary Wage Ceiling is $8,000); the same tax as A1.
#ASSERT `the income tax of` `F1` EQUALS 1040
-- F2: $8,000 a month in 2026: CPF 20% of 8,000 = 1,600 a month = 19,200. Reliefs 1,000 + 19,200; chargeable 96,000 - 20,200 = 75,800: 550 on the first 40,000 + 7% of 35,800 = 2,506: 3,056.
#ASSERT `the income tax of` `F2` EQUALS 3056

#ASSERT `the employee CPF of` `F2` EQUALS 19200

§§ `The cliffs: what one more dollar of a threshold's figure costs`

-- G1: the spouse relief limit. The earner of A2 with a spouse whose income is $8,000 and then $8,001 (s 39(2)(a)). The relief of $2,000 is lost, and the tax
-- rises by what 2,000 of chargeable income costs where the earner stands, across the 80,000 band edge: 760 x 7% + 1,240 x 11.5% = 53.20 + 142.60 = 195.80.
#ASSERT (`the income tax of` `G1b`) MINUS (`the income tax of` `G1a`) EQUALS (195 + 0.8)
-- G2: the child's income limit (Fifth Schedule para 3B: "exceeded $8,000"). Chargeable income moves from 43,000 to 47,000: 4,000 x 7% = 280.
#ASSERT (`the income tax of` `G2b`) MINUS (`the income tax of` `G2a`) EQUALS 280
-- G3: the parent's income limit (s 39(2)(i)(iv)): $9,000 is lost when the parent's income passes $8,000. Chargeable income moves from 38,000 to 47,000:
-- tax 200 + 8,000 x 3.5% = 480 becomes 1,040: 560.
#ASSERT (`the income tax of` `G3b`) MINUS (`the income tax of` `G3a`) EQUALS 560
-- G4: the CPF phase-in. From $500 to $750 a month the employee pays 0.6 of each extra dollar: 12 x (0.6 x 250) = 1,800 more for $250 more a month, and then
-- 20% of the whole wage, which at $750 is the same 150 (the bands meet); the next dollar costs 0.20 (150.2, the fraction ignored) so nothing: 1,800 again.
#ASSERT (`the employee CPF of` `G4_w750`) MINUS (`the employee CPF of` `G4_w500`) EQUALS 1800
#ASSERT (`the employee CPF of` `G4_w751`) MINUS (`the employee CPF of` `G4_w750`) EQUALS 0
-- G5: the Ordinary Wage Ceiling. Above $7,400 a month nothing more is taken for CPF in 2025.
#ASSERT (`the employee CPF of` `G4_w7401`) MINUS (`the employee CPF of` `G4_w7400`) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT (`the employee CPF of` `G4_w8000b`) MINUS (`the employee CPF of` `G4_w7400`) EQUALS 0
-- G6: the earned income relief steps up at 55. A man aged 54 (born 1971, A1's pay) has relief of $1,000, tax 1,040; aged 55 (A6) $6,000, tax 690: 350 less.
#ASSERT (`the income tax of` `G6`) MINUS (`the income tax of` `A6`) EQUALS 350

§§ `Cases the IRAS worked examples raised, settled from the Act`

-- H1 (fork H3): the first child, born 2008, is in full-time instruction but has income of $9,000, so Fifth Schedule para 3B allows nothing for her; the second child, born 2020,
-- is the mother's second child within s 39(2)(e) (para 7(b) leaves the ranking to the Comptroller, whose published example counts the first). Working mother's child relief for
-- the second child: 20% of 100,000 = 20,000 (para 5(1A)(d): the date is before 1 January 2024), and qualifying child relief 4,000 for her only. The mother: CPF 17,760; reliefs
-- 1,000 + 17,760 + 4,000 + 20,000 = 42,760; chargeable 57,240: 550 + 7% of 17,240 = 1,206.80: 1,756.80. (If the barred child did not count, the relief would be 15% = 15,000 and the tax 2,106.80.)
#ASSERT `the income tax of` `H1` EQUALS (1756 + 0.8)
-- H2: a child born in 2025, the qualifying child relief all the first adult's but the parenthood rebate shared equally (s 42A(2C): "in such proportion as they may agree"): $5,000 for a first
-- child, so $2,500 against each adult's tax. Each adult pays 9,036 and 9,636 before the rebate (the first has the 4,000 relief): 6,536 and 7,136, together 13,672.
#ASSERT `the income tax of` `H2` EQUALS 13672
-- H2 again: the first adult uses 2,500 of the rebate, not 5,000.
#ASSERT `the parenthood rebate used by the first adult of` `H2` EQUALS 2500
